      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A 26 April 1898 explosion at the powder works killed 13 people and forced the abandonment of nearby employee housing and a public school.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise_Park%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After the powder works closed, the settlement was renamed Paradise Park, a name that stuck for the community that grew around it.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://noehill.com/santacruz/nat2015000279.asp",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the late 19th century, a village of about one hundred residents had settled south of the powder manufactory, forming the core of modern Paradise Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
